3. In its reply filed on behalf of respondent no. 1 and 2, it is stated inter alia that the said accident was not occurred by the negligent driving of the respondent no.1 and not by the involvement of the Omvati And Anr vs Sh. Ashok Kumar And Anr on 4 December, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/78134301/
2 vehicle of respondent no.2 and they were wrongly implicated by the petitioners in the present case;
that the driver of the vehicle no. UP82S6030 had a valid and effective driving license at the time of alleged accident and the vehicle of respondent no. 2 was insured; that claim of the petitioner against the answering respondents are based on false and fabricated story and present claim petition is liable to be dismissed.

He further stated that the deceased was dragged and fell down at a distance of about 10 feet after being hit by the motorcycle; that the deceased fell down on the same side of the road where he was standing; that there was no much traffic on the road as it was 8:30 pm; that after the accident,
he stayed at the spot for about 5 minutes; that there were about 20 persons gathered at the spot;
that the police did not come to the spot in his presence; that respondent no.1 fled away from the spot after the accident; that the number of the motorcycle was seen by him; that he had noted down the vehicle number in his pocket dairy.
